{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &Self::NodeId) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<Self::NodeId>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.domain`.\n\n**Obligations.** The requirement has four parts:\n- A domain implements `Domain`.\n- A domain is `Clone + Send + Sync` and safe to share between executions.\n- The associated types carry the stated bounds: `Error: Send`, `NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`, `NodeContent: NodeContents`, and `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`.\n- The five methods have the stated shapes: `node_path`, `node_content`, `outgoing_edges`, and the two storage methods `load_evidence` and `store_evidence`. The storage futures are `Send`.\n\n**Trait shape and bounds.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` covers these.\n- It implements `Domain` for a fixture whose `NodeId` and `EdgeLabel` are opaque. They lack `Debug` and similar traits.\n- The fixture's `Error` is `Send` but not `Sync`, because it holds a `Cell`. It also isn't `Debug`, `Clone` or `std::error::Error`. A tightened bound would stop the fixture compiling.\n- The generic `check_bounds<G: Domain>` helper requires `G: Clone + Send + Sync`, `NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`, `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`, `Error: Send` and `NodeContent: NodeContents + Send + Sync`. A loosened bound would stop it compiling.\n- The `NodeContent` check is consistent with the spec. The `NodeContents` trait has `Send + Sync` supertraits (I confirmed this in `domain.rs`).\n- The helper wraps the `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` futures in `send(...)`, so a non-`Send` future would not compile.\n- The test calls and asserts `node_path` (segments, and different nodes give different paths).\n- It calls and asserts `outgoing_edges` (order, duplicates, empty results, and an error that is `Send`).\n- It also calls `node_content` and checks its format and fingerprint, and it exercises `load_evidence` and `store_evidence`.\n\n**Cloneable and shareable between executions.** Several tests use a cloned domain across concurrent executions.\n- `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` in `tests/contracts.rs` clones the domain and runs two executions concurrently through a barrier. It then checks that each execution's record and dependencies are independent.\n- `concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces` in `validation_tests.rs` runs three concurrent validations on a cloned domain. It asserts a peak concurrency of 3 and separate per-node traces.\n- `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads` in `agent/tests.rs` and `shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls` in `validation_tests.rs` share one domain across concurrent calls.\n\n**Real-domain use.** These tests run real domain implementations through the whole SDK, which supports the claim that every application domain implements `Domain`:\n- `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`\n- `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent`\n- `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer`\n- `later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace`\n- `domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement` in `src/sdk.rs`\n\nI found no gap. The \"introduce its members one capability at a time\" clause is prose. The individual members have their own requirements, and the tests marked for those requirements cover them.",
